Package: PaPeR
Type: Package
Title: Parentage Assignment for Multiallelic (Microhaplotype) Markers
Version: 0.1.0
Author: PaPeR Authors
Maintainer: PaPeR Authors <wittman98@gmail.com>
Description: Assigns dams and sires to genotyped individuals from
    microhaplotype or SNP genotypes and life-history data. Each parent slot is
    decided by a likelihood comparison of the assigned parents against
    alternative relationships (siblings, grandparents, aunts and uncles,
    half-siblings and others), with genotype messages from already assigned
    relatives. Error rates use a dropout/foreign model for microhaplotypes or
    the Sequoia error model for SNPs, and can be calibrated from the confident
    trios of the inferred pedigree. Sibship clustering and dummy parents are
    outside its scope.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
LinkingTo: Rcpp
Imports: Rcpp, stats
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), withr, CKMRsim, sequoia
